  "summary": "I added a \"Close portal\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`. It passed `typecheck`, but I haven't run it in a browser or clicked the button. Clicking it hides the energy disc, the halo glow behind the disc, and all particles. It also hides the platform ritual circle and the inner glowing ring, and drops the portal lights to 5% of their intensity. `window.__TASK_STATE__.portalActive` becomes false and `particleCount` becomes 0. The label changes to \"Open portal\". Clicking again shows everything again, restores the lights and the count, and changes the label back to \"Close portal\". Particle updates pause while the portal is closed. The state is also written immediately on click, so it doesn't wait for the next frame."
